diff --git a/BasicBWT-API.md b/BasicBWT-API.md
index 34a791c..0ae13c3 100644
--- a/BasicBWT-API.md
+++ b/BasicBWT-API.md
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ The pure-Python readers in `MUS.MultiStringBWT` expose the same methods
 | `getCharAtIndex(index)` | BWT column symbol at one row |
 | `getOccurrenceOfCharAtIndex(sym, index)` | occurrence/rank of `sym` up to `index` |
 | `getSequenceDollarID(strIndex, returnOffset=False)` | dollar ID (read ID) owning a row; optionally the offset within the read |
-| `recoverString(strIndex, withIndex=False)` | recover `'$' + read` for a dollar ID; with `withIndex=True` also returns the BWT row indices of the rotations |
+| `recoverString(strIndex, withIndex=False)` | recover `'$' + read` for a dollar ID (`bytes` from the `MUSCython` loader, `str` from the pure-Python `MUS` loader); with `withIndex=True` also returns the BWT row indices of the rotations |
 
 ## Example
 
diff --git a/Constructing-the-MSBWT.md b/Constructing-the-MSBWT.md
index 38e83c5..0cfd12e 100644
--- a/Constructing-the-MSBWT.md
+++ b/Constructing-the-MSBWT.md
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@ the original package:
 Both routes support uniform-length reads (`-u`) and nonuniform reads
 (no flag), and plain or gzip-compressed FASTQ.
 
+FASTQ is read as 4-line records.  If a file ends partway through a record
+(its line count is not a multiple of 4), construction stops with
+`Truncated FASTQ input '<file>' ...` and a nonzero exit code instead of
+building from the incomplete data.  Discard the output directory and fix or
+re-transfer the input.
+
 ## Two-step construction
 
 ```bash
@@ -107,8 +113,9 @@ documented in the legacy bug tracker in the main repository):
 - `convert` silently drops everything after the first newline of the
   input (exit 0);
 - `convert` reports an invalid symbol before the first newline as a
-  masked `TypeError: cannot concatenate 'str' and 'int' objects`
-  (exit 1).
+  masked `TypeError` (exit 1).  The message text depends on the Python
+  version: `cannot concatenate 'str' and 'int' objects` on Python 2,
+  `can only concatenate str (not "int") to str` on Python 3.
 
 ## Command summary
 
diff --git a/Persistent-Files-and-Compatibility.md b/Persistent-Files-and-Compatibility.md
index 0242e44..c804922 100644
--- a/Persistent-Files-and-Compatibility.md
+++ b/Persistent-Files-and-Compatibility.md
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ optional       an added layer; absence does not affect legacy behavior
 | `fmIndex.npy` | derived/cache | byte-reader FM index; rebuilt by the reader (verified by the Q1 audit's cache-regeneration family) |
 | `comp_fmIndex.npy` | derived/cache | compressed-reader FM index; rebuilt on demand |
 | `comp_refIndex.npy` | derived/cache | compressed-reader reference index; rebuilt on demand |
+| `totalCounts.p` | derived/cache | per-symbol totals, stored as a pickle of a 1-D NumPy array (integers for byte indexes, float64 for RLE); rebuilt when missing.  `msbwt-modern3` loads it with a restricted reader that refuses anything but a plain numeric array, so an untrusted or tampered file is rejected with an error rather than executed; delete it to have it regenerated |
 
 ## Two-source provenance (Feature 1)
 
diff --git a/Queries-with-the-Python-API.md b/Queries-with-the-Python-API.md
index 5df46e7..ff2a62d 100644
--- a/Queries-with-the-Python-API.md
+++ b/Queries-with-the-Python-API.md
@@ -48,7 +48,8 @@ reads:
 # dollar ID of the read owning a row
 dollar_id = bwt.getSequenceDollarID(row_index)
 
-# recover the read as '$' + read bytes
+# recover the read as '$' + read
+# (bytes from the MUSCython loader, str from the pure-Python MUS loader)
 seq = bwt.recoverString(dollar_id)
 
 # with the BWT row indices of each rotation
